## Section 4 — On-page SEO

# On-Page SEO

**Intent:** Optimize individual pages to rank and convert — titles, content, structure, internal links. Skip for off-page/backlinks (`off-page-seo.mdc`) or AI citation strategy (`ai-seo.mdc`).

## Before you optimize

1. Pick **one primary keyword** + search intent (informational, commercial, transactional).
2. Run `site:yourdomain.com "keyword"` — if multiple pages compete, fix cannibalization first (merge, redirect, or retarget).
3. Confirm page is **indexable** in Google Search Console (not blocked, not noindex, in sitemap).
4. If diagnosing a drop, audit in order: **crawlability → speed → on-page → content quality → links**. Don't tweak titles if Google can't index the page.

## Page elements checklist

| Element | Rule |
|---------|------|
| Title | Unique, 50–60 chars, primary keyword near start, compelling |
| Meta description | Unique, 150–160 chars, value prop + CTA |
| H1 | Exactly one; matches title/URL intent |
| H2/H3 | Logical hierarchy; no skipped levels for styling only |
| Opening | Primary topic in first ~100 words; no keyword stuffing |
| URL | Short, readable, hyphens, lowercase; keyword where natural |
| Images | Descriptive alt text, WebP where possible, lazy-load below fold |
| Canonical | Self-referencing on unique pages; HTTPS + www consistency |

## SPA & SSR patterns (production lessons)

From shipping production SPA keyword landings and SSR web applications:

| Situation | Do this |
|-----------|---------|
| **Hash routes** (`#page`) | Google often indexes one URL — **path URLs** for keyword landings; client-side redirect legacy hashes to paths |
| **SPA without SSR** | Static defaults in `index.html` + runtime `applyPageSeo()`; **post-build prerender** per path with unique title/meta/canonical in `dist/<path>/index.html` |
| **SSR / TanStack / Next** | Per-route `head()` / metadata API — no prerender needed if HTML ships unique tags server-side |
| **Single source of truth** | Central `seo.js` / `seo.ts`: `PAGE_SEO`, `LANDING_SEO`, keyword map — routes and sitemap import from it |
| **Sitemap** | List **path** canonicals only — never `#fragments` for landing pages |
| **JSON-LD** | `WebSite` + `Organization` sitewide; `FAQPage` on hub; `Article` / `WebApplication` on tools — verify in Rich Results Test, not `curl` alone |
| **Visible copy** | Keyword H1 + H2 hub blocks + FAQ on home/hub — not meta-only; one keyword → one canonical page |
| **Utility pages** | `noindex` favorites, reminders, account — keep out of sitemap |
| **Tests** | Unit: canonical paths, sitemap entries, seo module exports; E2E: path loads, legacy redirect, no `pageerror` |
| **Post-deploy** | GSC sitemap resubmit, cache purge (CDN shell), Rich Results spot-check |

**Cannibalization rule:** maintain a keyword → canonical URL table; strengthen assigned page instead of duplicating.

## Content quality

- Answer the query **above the fold** — then add depth.
- Beat top 3 competitors on usefulness, not word count alone.
- **E-E-A-T:** named author, cited sources, visible "last updated" date, about/contact pages.
- Avoid doorway pages, thin tag/category pages, duplicate/near-duplicate content.
- For scaled/programmatic pages: every URL needs **unique value**, not swapped variables only.

## Internal linking

- No orphan pages — every important URL reachable from nav or hub pages within **3 clicks** of home.
- Use **descriptive anchor text**; avoid exact-match spam.
- Hub-and-spoke for page sets: category hub → spoke pages → cross-links between related spokes.
- Link high-priority pages from higher-traffic pages.

## Schema caveat

Static HTML fetch and `curl` often **miss JS-injected JSON-LD** (Yoast, RankMath, etc.). Verify schema with [Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results) or rendered DOM — never report "no schema" from fetch alone.

## Output formats

**Pre-ship checklist** — emit as checkboxes before publishing any new/updated page.

**Audit findings** — table columns: Issue | Impact (H/M/L) | Evidence | Fix | Priority (1–5).

## Your routine

- **Weekly:** GSC → Performance → queries with impressions but low CTR → rewrite titles/metas.
- **Monthly:** Refresh top 10 pages; re-check cannibalization; fix broken internal links.

## Free tools

Google Search Console, PageSpeed Insights, Rich Results Test, Mobile-Friendly Test.

