## Before you audit **[core]**

1. Read `.agents/product-marketing.md` if present — business goals, priority keywords/topics.
2. Gather (ask if missing):
   - Site type (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, local, multilingual)
   - Known issues, recent migrations or redesigns
   - Scope: full site vs specific sections
   - GSC / analytics access (or best available evidence)

3. **Do not** start with title tweaks if crawlability or indexation is broken.

---

## Audit priority order **[core]**

1. **Crawlability & indexation** — can Google find and index pages?
2. **Technical foundations** — fast, secure, mobile-ready?
3. **On-page optimization** — titles, headings, content alignment?
4. **Content quality** — does it deserve to rank (E-E-A-T, depth)?
5. **Authority & links** — off-site credibility?

---

## Schema detection caveat **[core]**

`curl` and static fetches often **miss JS-injected JSON-LD** (Yoast, RankMath, SPA `useEffect`). Never report "no schema" from fetch alone.

Verify with: [Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results), rendered DOM, or Screaming Frog with JS rendering.

---

## Technical SEO **[core]**

### Crawlability
- `robots.txt` — no accidental blocks; sitemap reference present
- XML sitemap — canonical indexable URLs only; submitted to GSC
- Architecture — important pages within 3 clicks; no orphans
- `[applicable if large site]` Crawl budget — params, faceted nav, infinite scroll fallbacks

### Indexation
- `site:domain.com` vs expected URL count
- GSC coverage — noindex on money pages, wrong canonicals, redirect chains, soft 404s
- HTTPS + www/non-www + trailing slash consistency

### Speed & Core Web Vitals
- LCP < 2.5s, INP < 200ms, CLS < 0.1
- TTFB, images, JS weight, caching, CDN

### Mobile & security
- Responsive (not separate m. site); tap targets; same content as desktop
- HTTPS sitewide; no mixed content

---

## International SEO `[applicable if multilingual]`

- Hreflang: self-reference, reciprocal tags, valid ISO codes, `x-default`
- Each locale self-canonical — never cross-locale canonical to English
- Fully translated main content — not boilerplate-only locales
- Thin locale pages can drag site-wide quality — don't create locales you can't make helpful

---

## On-page & content (audit lens) **[core]**

Flag issues; detailed fix patterns → `seo-gtm.mdc`.

| Area | Check |
|------|-------|
| Titles / metas | Unique, length, keyword alignment, CTR-worthy |
| Headings | One H1; logical hierarchy |
| Content | Intent match, depth vs top 3, thin/doorway pages |
| Images | Alt text, compression, modern formats |
| Internal links | Important pages linked; descriptive anchors; cannibalization |
| E-E-A-T | Author, sources, about/contact, freshness |

---

## Site-type quick hits `[applicable if type matches]`

| Type | Common gaps |
|------|-------------|
| SaaS | Thin product/feature pages; blog disconnected from product; missing comparison/alternative pages |
| E-commerce | Thin categories; duplicate descriptions; faceted duplicates; missing product schema |
| Content/blog | Outdated posts; cannibalization; weak topical clusters |
| Local | NAP inconsistency; missing LocalBusiness schema; weak location content |

